<% content_for :title, "Nyika Village Registry" %>

<div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-6 shadow-sm">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-nyika-ink">Nyika Village Registry</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">Register once. Access programmes. Mobilise transparently.</p>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-700">
    <p>
      This is the household register for Nyika village. It keeps one record per
      household so that a family does not have to repeat their details for every
      programme.
    </p>

    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-100 p-4">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Are you a resident?</h2>
      <p class="mt-1">
        To check or update your household details, open the personal link the
        village office sent you. There is nothing to sign up for and no password
        to remember.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2">
        If you do not have your link, or it no longer works, speak to the village
        office and they will send you a new one.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-xl bg-slate-100 p-4">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-slate-900">What we record, and what we do not</h2>
      <ul class="mt-1 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5">
        <li>We record your household name, who lives there, and how to find and contact you.</li>
        <li>We record an age band, not a date of birth.</li>
        <li>We describe where you live in words. We do not record land or plot claims.</li>
        <li>We do not record national ID numbers, health details or income.</li>
        <li>You agree to each use separately. Agreeing to one is never agreeing to all.</li>
        <li>Every change is recorded with who made it, when, and why. Nothing is quietly deleted.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="mt-6 text-sm">
    <%= link_to "Village office sign in", new_user_session_path,
                class: "font-medium text-nyika-accent underline underline-offset-2" %>
  </p>
</div>
